{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/357573-possible-benefits-for-high-azoth","id":357573,"title":"Possible benefits for high Azoth.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-02T10:15:19-08:00","id":357573,"title":"Possible benefits for high Azoth.","content":"Feedback is very appreciated.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Transhuman Potential: at Azoth 6, each point of pyros spent grants +2 to any Attribute for a turn instead of +1. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Advanced Bestowments: these benefits are automatically gained when a promethean reaches Azoth 6.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ephemeral Flesh: spending pyros is no longer necessary to activate this Bestowment. You may spend 1 pyros so that spiritual weapons or armor grant an additional equipment bonus equal to Azoth/2 round up and an additional 1/1 armor, respectively (lasts for 1 scene).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Orphean Song: the Presence + Azoth roll for this Bestowment now has the 8 Again bonus, and an Exceptional Success makes the ephemeral being sleep for up to Azoth/2 round up in days.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unholy Strength: Strength rolls now gain the 8 Again bonus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Spare Parts: a point of pyros is no longer required and the Dexterity + Medicine rolls only take 15 minutes each. Also, surgical tools are no longer needed: the Promethean only needs to acquire the desired limbs and then attaches them like they are covered in glue. Wounds are still healed, but the limbs and changes in Physical Attributes can only be used once the five successes are accumulated. Using the limbs before that results in a chance die.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mesmerizing Appearance: Social rolls involving beauty now gain the 8 Again bonus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Heart Of Stone: the character no longer needs to go to sleep to activate this Bestowment, and she may take on a different appearance each time. Also, damage received while in this form is now lethal instead of aggravated. Lastly, she may roll Wits + Azoth to sense her surroundings normally for one turn. How often she can perceive her surroundings normally is decided by the ST.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Corpse Tongue: the character may use this Bestowment on the same corpse twice instead of once. Also, if spending 1 pyros to get an answer more complex than a yes or no, more details are received.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unholy Stamina: rolls involving Stamina now gain the 8 Again bonus. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unbreakable Will: rolls involving Resolve now gain the 8 Again bonus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Re-Animator: only 2 pyros is spent per corpse. Each zombie starts with Power 2, Finesse 2 and Resistance 4. Their Speed is equal to Power + Finesse. Defense is equal to Finesse. Willpower is equal to Resistance. They don't lose limbs due to damage, but are still vulnerable to damage to the brain. Each success on the Presence + Azoth roll can add 2 dots to the zombie's traits, up to a maximum of 5 for each. They now deal lethal damage with a bite, but they must succeed on a grapple roll first.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Victim Shadow: you may now move while you are a shadow. You make Dexterity or Wits + Stealth rolls as normal, but with a +2 bonus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Radioactive Affinity: each point of radioactive &quot;damage&quot; the fully healed character takes grants him 2 points of pyros.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T17:12:13-08:00","id":357904,"title":"","content":"I like the basic line of thought, but a bunch of the benefits you pressent are identical to the benefits you would get through the Transmutation &quot;Rarified Bestowment&quot;.<br /> But I really like the general idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Kr